# Shell scripts are LF, ALWAYS. `#!/usr/bin/env bash` followed by CRLF makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter literally named "bash\r", and every `case`/`in`
# line becomes a syntax error. The vendored tests/_kit/run-automated-tests.sh is
# the file this protects (automated-tests-§2).
*.sh   text eol=lf
